  "title": "Que (province)",
  "provenance": "Pleiades",
  "placeTypeURIs": [
    "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/place-types/province-2"
  ],
  "details": "<p>During the time of Sargon II (r. 721-705 BC), the governor of the province of Que carried out campaigns against Mita of Mu\u0161ku (= King Midas of Phrygia). As a province, Que is mentioned in administrative texts from the reign of Sargon. Its governor is also mentioned in royal correspondence of this king and that of his grandson Esarhaddon (r. 680-669 BC). A tax official from Que is mentioned in a dated administrative text from the time of Ashurbanipal (r. 668-ca. 631 BC). During the reigns of Ashurbanipal and A\u0161\u0161ur-etel-il\u0101ni, governors of Que held the office of <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"https://www.ucl.ac.uk/sargon/eponymlistsandchronicles/\" target=\"_self\" title=\"\">eponym</a>.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Que became an Assyrian province during the reign of the eighth-century-BC Assyrian king Shalmaneser V (726-722 BC).",
